#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_emc_v1.py — fence EMC_V1_20261011
#
# New BACKTEST-ONLY strategy EMC_V1 ("Ember") — EMA 9/21 spot → option cross:
#
#   * On a NIFTY SPOT 5m candle close where EMA9 crosses EMA21 (up → CE,
#     down → PE), the weekly option of that side whose premium is inside
#     ₹150–200 is selected (highest premium if several; band / pick editable).
#   * The selected option is bought once ITS OWN 5m EMA9 is above (CE) /
#     below (PE) EMA21 — immediately if already so, else at the first 1m close
#     where it gets there (intrabar; "option candle close" mode available).
#   * Exits: SL / TP in option-premium points, optional trailing SL (trigger +
#     gap), the opposite spot cross (which also arms the other side), square-
#     off 15:15. No new entries from 14:30. Max trades/day and max LOSING
#     trades/day. One position at a time. All of it editable on the form.
#
#  NEW   backend/app/backtest/emc/{__init__,emc_v1_engine,backtest_emc_runner,test_emc_runner_sim}.py
#  EDIT  backend/app/api/backtest_routes.py        (allow-list + dispatch arm)
#        backend/app/backtest/queue_worker.py      (queue dispatch arm — the twin copy)
#        backend/app/backtest/replay/overlays.py   (Trade Replay: spot + option EMA lines)
#        backend/app/config/strategy_display.py    (codename Ember)
#        frontend/src/pages/Backtest.jsx           (chip, form, buildConfig, describeConfig, CSV diag)
#        frontend/src/pages/backtest/SweepBuilder.jsx (16 emc_* axes + lot compounding)
#        frontend/src/pages/backtest/paramFormat.js   (emcParamSummary)
#        frontend/src/pages/backtest/BacktestQueue.jsx / RunComparison.jsx (param line)
#        frontend/src/pages/backtest/Portfolio.jsx  (label + colour)
#        frontend/src/strategies/displayNames.js
#  Mirrored to desktop/src-tauri/{backend,frontend}/ when those trees exist.
#
#  No live/paper path touched, no schema change, no new dependency.
#  Gates before anything is kept: py_compile, esbuild parse of every edited
#  JS/JSX, the 97-check EMC suite (engine, scripted sessions, runner on the
#  replay suite's synthetic corpus, persisted-run → Trade Replay) and the
#  existing Trade Replay suite (overlays.py is edited). Any failure → every
#  file restored, new files removed.
#
# Usage: python3 apply_emc_v1.py [--repo PATH] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests] [--skip-esbuild]
# Run ONLY this script — it carries every payload itself.

